{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SoMCMCm5NvZNidwHJa9jcG","type":"tool_result","content":"=== CASUALTY ===\n5108:702.153. Casualty\n5110:702.153a Casualty is a keyword that represents two abilities. The first is a static ability that functions while the spell with casualty is on the stack. The second is a triggered ability that functions while the spell with casualty is on the stack. Casualty N means “As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power N or greater,” and “When you cast this spell, if a casualty cost was paid for it, copy it. If the spell has any targets, you may choose new targets for the copy.” Paying a spell’s casualty cost follows the rules for paying additional costs in rules 601.2b and 601.2f–h.\n5112:702.153b If a spell has multiple instances of casualty, each is paid separately and triggers based on the payments made for it, not any other instance of casualty.\n7340:Casualty\n7341:A keyword ability that allows you to sacrifice a creature to create a copy of a spell. See 702.153, “Casualty.”\n=== MIRACLE ===\n4668:702.94. Miracle\n4670:702.94a Miracle is a static ability linked to a triggered ability. (See rule 603.11.) “Miracle [cost]” means “You may reveal this card from your hand as you draw it if it’s the first card you’ve drawn this turn. When you reveal this card this way, you may cast it by paying [cost] rather than its mana cost.”\n4672:702.94b If a player chooses to reveal a card using its miracle ability, they play with that card revealed until that card leaves their hand, that ability resolves, or that ability otherwise leaves the stack. (See rule 701.20a.)\n8311:Miracle\n8312:A keyword ability that lets you cast a spell for a reduced cost if it’s the first card you draw in a turn. See rule 702.94, “Miracle.”\n=== CONVERGE (702.x) ===\n1495:207.2c An ability word appears in italics at the beginning of some abilities. Ability words are similar to keywords in that they tie together cards that have similar functionality, but they have no special rules meaning and no individual entries in the Comprehensive Rules. The ability words are adamant, addendum, alliance, battalion, bloodrush, celebration, channel, chroma, cohort, constellation, converge, council’s dilemma, coven, delirium, descend 4, descend 8, disappear, domain, eerie, eminence, enrage, fateful hour, fathomless descent, ferocious, flurry, formidable, grandeur, hellbent, heroic, imprint, infusion, inspired, join forces, kinship, landfall, lieutenant, magecraft, metalcraft, morbid, opus, pack tactics, paradox, parley, radiance, raid, rally, renew, repartee, revolt, secret council, spell mastery, strive, survival, sweep, tempting offer, threshold, undergrowth, valiant, vivid, void, and will of the council.\n=== AFFINITY ===\n4304:702.41. Affinity\n4306:702.41a Affinity is a static ability that functions while the spell with affinity is on the stack. “Affinity for [text]” means “This spell costs {1} less to cast for each [text] you control.”\n4308:702.41b If a spell has multiple instances of affinity, each of them applies.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a1b7c704-d004-4a3e-ade9-c0cdca9e5add","uuid":"ca9c02d8-7502-4fd0-9e29-ff429012e90a","timestamp":"2026-06-04T08:47:53.270Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== CASUALTY ===\n5108:702.153. Casualty\n5110:702.153a Casualty is a keyword that represents two abilities. The first is a static ability that functions while the spell with casualty is on the stack. The second is a triggered ability that functions while the spell with casualty is on the stack. Casualty N means “As an additional cost to cast this spell, you may sacrifice a creature with power N or greater,” and “When you cast this spell, if a casualty cost was paid for it, copy it. If the spell has any targets, you may choose new targets for the copy.” Paying a spell’s casualty cost follows the rules for paying additional costs in rules 601.2b and 601.2f–h.\n5112:702.153b If a spell has multiple instances of casualty, each is paid separately and triggers based on the payments made for it, not any other instance of casualty.\n7340:Casualty\n7341:A keyword ability that allows you to sacrifice a creature to create a copy of a spell. See 702.153, “Casualty.”\n=== MIRACLE ===\n4668:702.94. Miracle\n4670:702.94a Miracle is a static ability linked to a triggered ability. (See rule 603.11.) “Miracle [cost]” means “You may reveal this card from your hand as you draw it if it’s the first card you’ve drawn this turn. When you reveal this card this way, you may cast it by paying [cost] rather than its mana cost.”\n4672:702.94b If a player chooses to reveal a card using its miracle ability, they play with that card revealed until that card leaves their hand, that ability resolves, or that ability otherwise leaves the stack. (See rule 701.20a.)\n8311:Miracle\n8312:A keyword ability that lets you cast a spell for a reduced cost if it’s the first card you draw in a turn. See rule 702.94, “Miracle.”\n=== CONVERGE (702.x) ===\n1495:207.2c An ability word appears in italics at the beginning of some abilities. Ability words are similar to keywords in that they tie together cards that have similar functionality, but they have no special rules meaning and no individual entries in the Comprehensive Rules. The ability words are adamant, addendum, alliance, battalion, bloodrush, celebration, channel, chroma, cohort, constellation, converge, council’s dilemma, coven, delirium, descend 4, descend 8, disappear, domain, eerie, eminence, enrage, fateful hour, fathomless descent, ferocious, flurry, formidable, grandeur, hellbent, heroic, imprint, infusion, inspired, join forces, kinship, landfall, lieutenant, magecraft, metalcraft, morbid, opus, pack tactics, paradox, parley, radiance, raid, rally, renew, repartee, revolt, secret council, spell mastery, strive, survival, sweep, tempting offer, threshold, undergrowth, valiant, vivid, void, and will of the council.\n=== AFFINITY ===\n4304:702.41. Affinity\n4306:702.41a Affinity is a static ability that functions while the spell with affinity is on the stack. “Affinity for [text]” means “This spell costs {1} less to cast for each [text] you control.”\n4308:702.41b If a spell has multiple instances of affinity, each of them applies.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
