s_drawn_this_turn == 1`.\n   - Solved skip-turns (Gap H) and pragmatic coin flips (via player.choose_yes_no for testability).\n   - Solved sos_257 animation persistence (continuous effect must re-assert CREATURE/Wizard/PT each apply_all since cleanup resets characteristics) and noted restricted-mana (\"only for I/S\") is not enforceable without mana tagging — documented as a limitation.\n   - Solved sos_13 mana_cost parsing: spec is \"{1}{W}{W} // {W}\" which ManaCost.parse can't handle — hard-code the creature side \"{1}{W}{W}\".\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - (System task prompt) \"# Phase 1 of 2 — PLANNING ... You are the planning agent. You will not write any implementation code in this phase. A separate implementation agent runs next, in a fresh session, and inherits only the file `/workspace/PLAN.md`... Do not edit any cards/sos/<id>/card_impl.py or engine/ file in this phase. Planning only.\" Followed by the task: \"Implement the following SOS cards: 1, 4, 13, 57, 97, 120, 201, 226, 245, 257 in `/workspace/cards/sos/`... Use the completed FDN cards... Refer to RULEBOOK.txt... You are expected to make changes to the engine to implement new keywords and mechanics... **Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/.** These tests are staged for your local verification only; the runner uses its own authoritative copies for grading. Modifying the workspace tests will not change your score.\"\n   - (Final message) \"CRITICAL: Respond with TEXT ONLY. Do NOT call any tools... Your task is to create a detailed summary of the conversation so far...\" (this summary request)\n\n   Security/constraint instructions to preserve verbatim (from task + AGENTS.md):\n   - \"Do not edit any cards/sos/<id>/card_impl.py or engine/ file in this phase. Planning only.\"\n   - \"Do not modify any files under workspace/engine_tests/.\"\n   - \"Treat engine_tests/ as read-only: do not modify, add to, or delete files in it. Likewise do not modify or delete any existing FDN reference test file at cards/fdn/fdn_*/tests.py.\"\n   - \"Additive-only engine modifications — You may add new methods, classes, helpers, and files inside engine/. You may modify the bodies of existing functions... You MUST NOT rename, move, or delete anything that already exists in engine/.\"\n   - \"Card location invariant — Each card's canonical implementation class must remain in cards/sos/{card_id}/card_impl.py.\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - None outstanding for the PLANNING phase. PLAN.md has been written with all three required sections. The implementation itself is explicitly the job of a SEPARATE agent in a fresh session, NOT this planning agent.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary request, I completed and saved `/workspace/PLAN.md` using the Write tool. The tool returned \"File created successfully at: /workspace/PLAN.md\". The PLAN.md contains: a \"0. KEY ENGINE FACTS\" section (non-obvious engine behaviors), \"1. ENGINE GAPS\" table (gaps A–H with smallest change, file/seam, and cards reusing each), \"2. PER-CARD PLANS\" (detailed plans for all 10 cards: sos_4, sos_245, sos_57, sos_1, sos_226, sos_120, sos_201, sos_13, sos_97, sos_257 — each with base class setup, oracle clauses, nearest FDN analogue, exact seams, edge cases), and \"3. IMPLEMENTATION ORDER\" (Phase 0 engine seams first, then Phases 1–4 grouping cards simplest→hardest with rationale). The planning deliverable is complete.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   The PLANNING phase task is concluded — the sole deliverable (PLAN.md) has been written. No further action is in line with the user's request without explicit confirmation, since the implementation is reserved for a separate fresh-session agent and this agent was instructed \"You will not write any implementation code in this phase.\" If the user wants revisions to PLAN.md, that would be the only natural continuation. No next step should be taken without user confirmation.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (li